    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: For Area, use a simple function such as f(x)=x^2 or f(x)=2x+1. Apply the definition step by step, then compare the answer with the graph.\nExample 2 - Contrast: A similar-looking problem can be wrong if it breaks the condition, unit, order, or definition.\nExample 3 - Application: Use Area with speed changes, filling water, area under a graph, or motion along a road.\nVisual Model: Show the idea using a number line, curve, tangent, area strip, or limit picture and explain what each part represents.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Area studies change, closeness, or accumulated value. A graph helps you see the meaning before using symbols.",
    "advancedExplanation": "Area connects local change, limiting behavior, approximation, or accumulation. Advanced analysis makes this precise using functions, convergence, continuity, differentiability, or integration conditions.",
    "practicePrompt": "Create one example for Area. Solve it step by step, show a quick check, and explain one common mistake a student might make.",
