    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: Uniform convergence of derivatives can control derivative of the limit.\nExample 2 - Contrast: Use uniform convergence or a theorem with the correct hypotheses before interchanging limits.\nExample 3 - Application: It is used in analysis, approximation, power series, differential equations, and numerical methods.\nVisual Understanding: Imagine a whole graph moving toward another graph, then check whether all points get close together.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Interchange limit and derivative studies change, closeness, or accumulated value. A graph helps you see the meaning before using symbols.",
