    "id": "ug-year-3__operations-research__optimization__dynamic-programming-introduction",
    "classLevel": "UG Year 3",
    "chapter": "Operations Research",
    "topic": "Optimization",
    "subtopic": "Dynamic programming introduction",
    "introduction": "Dynamic programming introduction is an operations-research idea. It helps choose good decisions under constraints, costs, or uncertainty.",
    "detailedExplanation": "Basic Idea: Dynamic programming solves a problem by combining solutions of overlapping subproblems.\n\nHow It Works: Define variables, objective, constraints, and method before computing or optimizing.\n\nWhy It Works: Optimization works by comparing feasible choices using a clear mathematical rule.\n\nWhere We Use It: It is used in transport, scheduling, staffing, logistics, games, and service systems.\n\nCommon mistake: Optimizing a value before checking whether the choice is feasible.\n\nCorrect idea: Feasibility comes first; optimization compares only allowed choices.\n\nPrinciple: Dynamic programming solves a problem by combining solutions of overlapping subproblems.\n\nWorked Example: Fibonacci recurrence F_n=F_(n-1)+F_(n-2) stores earlier values.\n\nVerification: Stored values avoid repeated work.\n\n**Key Point:** Dynamic programming solves a problem by combining solutions of overlapping subproblems.",
    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: Fibonacci recurrence F_n=F_(n-1)+F_(n-2) stores earlier values.\nExample 2 - Contrast: Feasibility comes first; optimization compares only allowed choices.\nExample 3 - Application: It is used in transport, scheduling, staffing, logistics, games, and service systems.\nVisual Understanding: Use a feasible region, network, table, decision tree, or payoff matrix.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Dynamic programming remembers smaller answers.",
    "advancedExplanation": "Bellman's principle of optimality guides many DP problems.",
    "practicePrompt": "Compute Fibonacci numbers up to F_6 using stored values.",
    "updatedAt": 1786245296137
  },
