    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: For Simplicial complexes, test the idea on f(x)=x^2, e^x, or a simple interval. Check the analytic condition before using the theorem.\nExample 2 - Contrast: If the required condition is missing, Simplicial complexes may not apply even when the notation looks similar.\nExample 3 - Application: In Topology, this topic helps decide whether a calculation, model, theorem, or algorithm is valid.\nVisual Model: Use a small diagram, table, graph, or symbolic example that shows the exact object involved in Simplicial complexes.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Simplicial complexes is easiest when you attach it to one small example. Name the setting, check the condition, then use the rule only for that setting.",
