    "introduction": "Econometrics theory interface is an advanced idea in Mathematical Economics. It gives precise language for a research question, model, proof, or method. Learning it helps students judge claims carefully instead of trusting vague similarity.",
    "detailedExplanation": "Basic Idea: The econometrics theory interface links economic models with statistical identification and estimation.\n\nHow It Works: First state the objects. Next write the assumptions clearly. Then use the definition only when those assumptions are satisfied.\n\nWhy It Works: Research mathematics depends on exact conditions. If a condition is missing, the same method can give a false conclusion.\n\nWhere We Use It: It is used in Interdisciplinary Mathematics for modelling, algorithms, proofs, communication, or research design.\n\nCommon mistake: Using a powerful idea without checking its definitions, limits, or data assumptions.\n\nCorrect idea: Check the setting, test a small example, and look for a counterexample before generalising.\n\nDefinition: The econometrics theory interface links economic models with statistical identification and estimation.\n\nWorked Example: A demand model needs assumptions before data can estimate causal effects.\n\nVerification: Compare with a known simple case, check assumptions, and confirm the conclusion follows.\n\nVisual Understanding: Picture payoff trees, equilibria, risk curves, and optimization diagrams. Notice which parts are inputs, rules, outputs, and limitations.\n\nMemory Trick: Use S-A-E: Setting, Assumption, Example.\n\n**Key Point:** The econometrics theory interface links economic models with statistical identification and estimation.",
    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: A demand model needs assumptions before data can estimate causal effects.\nExample 2 - Counterexample: Change one assumption and ask whether the conclusion still holds. If not, the assumption was essential.\nExample 3 - Application: This idea helps researchers make precise models, proofs, algorithms, or communication choices in Mathematical Economics.\nVisual Model: Use payoff trees, equilibria, risk curves, and optimization diagrams to keep the concept concrete before using formal notation.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Econometrics theory interface is not just a name. Learn the setting, the needed assumption, and one example. That makes the research idea easier to trust and use.",
    "advancedExplanation": "It checks whether observed data answer the theoretical question. At PhD level, the main skill is knowing the hypotheses, standard examples, limitations, and how the topic connects to nearby research areas.",
    "practicePrompt": "For Econometrics theory interface, write the main definition or principle, give one valid example, and explain one limitation or assumption that matters.",
