    "subtopic": "Research ethics",
    "introduction": "Research ethics is an advanced idea in Research Design and Communication. It gives precise language for a research question, model, proof, or method. Learning it helps students judge claims carefully instead of trusting vague similarity.",
    "detailedExplanation": "Basic Idea: Research ethics means honest credit, careful claims, transparent limitations, and responsible use of results.\n\nHow It Works: First state the objects. Next write the assumptions clearly. Then use the principle only when those assumptions are satisfied.\n\nWhy It Works: Research mathematics depends on exact conditions. If a condition is missing, the same method can give a false conclusion.\n\nWhere We Use It: It is used in Research Practice for modelling, algorithms, proofs, communication, or research design.\n\nCommon mistake: Using a powerful idea without checking its definitions, limits, or data assumptions.\n\nCorrect idea: Check the setting, test a small example, and look for a counterexample before generalising.\n\nPrinciple: Research ethics means honest credit, careful claims, transparent limitations, and responsible use of results.\n\nWorked Example: Citing sources and reporting failed assumptions are ethical duties.\n\nVerification: Compare with a known simple case, check assumptions, and confirm the conclusion follows.\n\nVisual Understanding: Picture papers, theorem statements, proof maps, examples, and reproducibility checklists. Notice which parts are inputs, rules, outputs, and limitations.\n\nMemory Trick: Use S-A-E: Setting, Assumption, Example.\n\n**Key Point:** Research ethics means honest credit, careful claims, transparent limitations, and responsible use of results.",
    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: Citing sources and reporting failed assumptions are ethical duties.\nExample 2 - Counterexample: Change one assumption and ask whether the conclusion still holds. If not, the assumption was essential.\nExample 3 - Application: This idea helps researchers make precise models, proofs, algorithms, or communication choices in Research Design and Communication.\nVisual Model: Use papers, theorem statements, proof maps, examples, and reproducibility checklists to keep the concept concrete before using formal notation.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Research ethics is not just a name. Learn the setting, the needed assumption, and one example. That makes the research idea easier to trust and use.",
    "advancedExplanation": "Mathematics depends on trust as well as proof. At PhD level, the main skill is knowing the hypotheses, standard examples, limitations, and how the topic connects to nearby research areas.",
    "practicePrompt": "For Research ethics, write the main definition or principle, give one valid example, and explain one limitation or assumption that matters.",
